        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "364ffc56-13ec-5156-afc5-4f65b62a9143",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jupp Heynckes\n- Organizations: Liverpool, Borussia Mönchengladbach, UEFA Executive Committee\n- Events: 1977 European Cup Final\n- Places: Stadio Olimpico, Rome, Italy, Bern, England, Germany\n\nFacts:\n- On 17 September 1976, the UEFA Executive Committee decided in Bern that the 1977 European Cup Final would be held at the Stadio Olimpico in Rome, Italy.\n- On 25 May 1977, the 1977 European Cup Final was an association football match between Liverpool of England and Borussia Mönchengladbach of Germany.\n- On 25 May 1977, Liverpool defeated Borussia Mönchengladbach in the 1977 European Cup Final.\n- During Jupp Heynckes's period with Borussia Mönchengladbach, the team reached its only European Cup final in 1977 and lost to Liverpool.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "02d7feef-a5bc-57ac-a605-b958f2b4b173",
        "text": "Page: Jupp Heynckes. Sentence: During this period, the team also played in its only European Cup final in 1977, losing to Liverpool.\nPage: 1977 European Cup Final. Sentence: The 1977 European Cup Final was an association football match between Liverpool of England and Borussia Mönchengladbach of Germany on 25 May 1977 at the Stadio Olimpico in Rome, Italy (the venue was decided in Bern by the UEFA Executive Committee on 17 September 1976).",
